{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1785092300,"nonce":"VZ8mKvkfJwKeqd5hrvtHuHVQxpY=","message":"Dependency update after the ADR-0061 s1/s2 scoping adjudication.\n\n\"Depends on: s2, s3\" is now more precise: this depends on **s2b** (the CSI\nephemeral inline volume + FUSE lazy lower layer, `0628369`) and on\n**s3-drain** (`7f05f39`), not on the s2/s3 as originally sliced. s3-feed —\nthe eager Scarab-owned fetcher that replaces the feed tunnel — does NOT\ncreate the writable upper layer, so it does not unblock this.\n\nThe prerequisite is specifically s2b's **overlay mount options**, because the\nupper layer this slice hashes is only trustworthy as a diff if the overlay is\nmounted with them:\n\n    mount -t overlay overlay \\\n      -o lowerdir=\u003cfuse-mnt\u003e,upperdir=\u003cup\u003e,workdir=\u003cwk\u003e,\\\n    index=off,metacopy=off,redirect_dir=off,xino=off \\\n      \u003ckubelet-target-path\u003e\n\nWhy each one matters to *this* slice, not just to s2b:\n\n- `metacopy=off` — with metacopy on, a metadata-only change copies the inode\n  up **without** its data, so the upper layer would contain entries this\n  slice would hash as changed content when the content did not change (and\n  worse, would have to go back to the lower layer to get the bytes). The diff\n  stops being self-contained.\n- `redirect_dir=off` — a redirected directory records its origin in a\n  `trusted.overlay.*` xattr instead of appearing as a normal upper entry, so\n  a renamed directory would not read as the set of paths it actually is.\n- `index=off` / `xino=off` — the FUSE lower's inode numbering is synthetic,\n  so any inode-identity-based upper/lower correlation is meaningless here.\n- Whiteouts (char device `0:0`) and opaque dirs\n  (`trusted.overlay.opaque=\"y\"`) are how deletions appear in the upper layer.\n  This slice must read both to compute the DELETED half of the diff — a\n  naive walk of `upperdir` that ignores them produces a tree that silently\n  resurrects deleted paths.\n- `upperdir`/`workdir` must not be tmpfs (trusted xattrs), which is why s2b\n  places them at `/var/lib/scarab/pods/\u003cpod-uid\u003e/{upper,work}` on the node\n  disk.\n\nAlso inherited from s7 (`dd67e12`): the new tree = parent tree + diff\ncomputation must preserve `mode` and `mtime_ms` on unchanged entries taken\nfrom the parent, and must NOT rewrite them. A tree hash moves when an mtime\nmoves, so a diff that \"helpfully\" restamps untouched entries would defeat the\nskip-if-unchanged comparison this slice exists to make cheap.","files":null}]}